#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:45
#: 87fd2c833fb6453a83909b2c3adb599f
msgid "§12.2 — 30/60/90-Day Action Checklist"
msgstr "§12.2 —— 30/60/90 天行动清单"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:47
#: 86e225b80b554cad99c7fda2ced435ab
msgid ""
"The book's single most important claim is that you do not need to adopt all "
"twelve cells at once. You pick **one**, ship it, ship the *column* or the "
"*row* it sits in, then run a full HarnessCard review. Below are the three "
"sub-tasks with hands-on pointers; a standalone copy lives at "
"`_handson/12-where-we-go-from-here/checklist-30-60-90.md`."
msgstr ""
"本书最重要的那一条主张是：你 *不必* 把十二格一次性全采纳。你挑 **一格**、把它交付、再把它所在的那一 *列* 或 *行* 交付，然后跑一轮完整的"
" HarnessCard 评审。下面是这三个子任务，带 hands-on 指针；独立副本放在 `_handson/12-where-we-go-"
"from-here/checklist-30-60-90.md`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:53
#: b51094cfddb345cd9cb06c098b2eff57
msgid "Day 1–30 · One Cell"
msgstr "Day 1–30 · 一格"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:55
#: 52546bf1952b44449c2cc666c8d00b47
msgid ""
"Pick one matrix cell, ship one artefact for it, run it against the "
"HarnessCard rubric from Appendix D."
msgstr "挑一格矩阵单元，为它交付一件制品，再拿附录 D 的 HarnessCard 评分尺跑一遍。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:58
#: 448a742e84424fdc891f95fe10883f1f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**SDD × Bridle.** Commit an `AGENTS.md` based on `_handson/05-harness-"
"anatomy/sdd-x-bridle/AGENTS.md.sample`; ties into {ref}`sdd-x-bridle`."
msgstr ""
"**SDD × 缰绳。** 以 `_handson/05-harness-anatomy/sdd-x-bridle/AGENTS.md.sample` "
"为底，提交一份 `AGENTS.md`；与 {ref}`sdd-x-bridle` 相挂钩。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:61
#: 83e91f1315b0473baf015086cf0613b0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**TDD × Fence.** Install a `PreToolUse` hook based on `_handson/05-harness-"
"anatomy/tdd-x-fence/hooks.json`; ties into {ref}`tdd-x-fence`."
msgstr ""
"**TDD × 护栏。** 以 `_handson/05-harness-anatomy/tdd-x-fence/hooks.json` 为底，装一条 "
"`PreToolUse` 钩子；与 {ref}`tdd-x-fence` 相挂钩。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:64
#: ad0d5448201543bfaeef7735dfe216bd
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**MDD × Fence.** Adopt a per-session cost cap from `_handson/05-harness-"
"anatomy/mdd-x-fence/cost-cap.yaml`; ties into {ref}`mdd-x-fence`."
msgstr ""
"**MDD × 护栏。** 采纳 `_handson/05-harness-anatomy/mdd-x-fence/cost-cap.yaml` "
"中那条\"单次会话成本上限\"；与 {ref}`mdd-x-fence` 相挂钩。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:68
#: 62debce1c2954628be66d5abcf81e8ff
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Ford, Parsons & Kua {cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary` supply the framing:"
" one fitness function at a time is already a real improvement."
msgstr ""
"Ford、Parsons 与 Kua {cite}`ford2017buildingevolutionary` 提供了这件事的大框架：一次只上一条 "
"fitness function，就已是一次真实的改进。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:71
#: 53122c42fdbd4716b9895fc681e97a96
msgid "Pitfall — The Day-30 \"we are done\" trap"
msgstr "陷阱 —— 第 30 天 \"我们搞完了\" 的坑"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:74
#: 9e47c67df98a4d7d8240481e36bd7fd3
msgid ""
"A team ships one cell by Day 30, celebrates, and stops. Ninety days later "
"the cell has decayed — no Groom job was added, no review cadence was "
"established, nobody owns the artefact. The +1 became +0.3 and is trending "
"toward zero. **Why**: a single cell is a seed, not a crop. The Day-30 "
"milestone exists to prove the team *can* ship a harness artefact; the Day-60"
" milestone exists to prove the team can *keep* one alive. Teams that skip "
"the second milestone end the quarter with the same harness theatre they "
"started with, minus a week of engineering time. **Fix**: the Day-30 exit "
"criterion is not \"artefact is merged\" but \"the artefact has an owner, a "
"review cadence, and one refused or measured event in its log\". An unused "
"cell is a rehearsal, not a production."
msgstr ""
"一支团队在第 30 天交付了一格，庆祝、然后停下来。九十天之后，这格已经腐化——没有 Groom "
"任务被加上、没有评审节奏被建立、没有人署名持有这件制品。那个 +1 变成 +0.3，并在往 0 "
"靠拢。**为什么**：单一格子是一粒种子，不是一茬庄稼。第 30 天的里程碑是为了证明这支团队 *能* 交付一件挽具制品；第 60 "
"天的里程碑则是为了证明这支团队 "
"*能让它活下来*。跳过第二个里程碑的团队，季末拿到的还是当初那场挽具剧场，只不过额外赔掉了一周工程师时间。**解法**：第 30 "
"天的出口判据不是\"制品已合并\"，而是\"这件制品有归属、有评审节奏、日志里至少有一次 refused 或 measured "
"事件\"。没被用起来的格子是排练，不是演出。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:89
#: b09dd1ce73944310b44e2b84be723e82
msgid "Day 31–60 · One Row or One Column"
msgstr "Day 31–60 · 一行，或一列"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:91
#: 151e8d2504ce4590af6df165fb280e4d
msgid ""
"Extend to a full row (one guardian across all four zones) or a full column "
"(one zone across all three guardians)."
msgstr "扩展到完整一行（一位护法横跨全部四个区域），或完整一列（一个区域横跨全部三位护法）。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:94
#: 6bfac46cf933401b91b27283aa2ebdac
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Full SDD row.** Ship Bridle + Fence + Paddock + Groom artefacts from "
"`_handson/05-harness-anatomy/sdd-x-*/`. Cells {ref}`sdd-x-bridle`, "
"{ref}`sdd-x-fence`, {ref}`sdd-x-paddock`, {ref}`sdd-x-groom`."
msgstr ""
"**完整 SDD 行。** 交付 `_handson/05-harness-anatomy/sdd-x-*/` 下的缰绳 ＋ 护栏 ＋ 牧场 ＋ 梳理 "
"四件制品。对应格子：{ref}`sdd-x-bridle`、{ref}`sdd-x-fence`、{ref}`sdd-x-"
"paddock`、{ref}`sdd-x-groom`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:98
#: d49c41a6c8bf4ce3b10c966c299c2da7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Full Fence column.** Ship SDD + TDD + MDD fences from "
"`_handson/05-harness-anatomy/*-x-fence/`. Cells {ref}`sdd-x-fence`, "
"{ref}`tdd-x-fence`, {ref}`mdd-x-fence`."
msgstr ""
"**完整护栏列。** 交付 `_handson/05-harness-anatomy/*-x-fence/` 下的 SDD ＋ TDD ＋ MDD "
"三道护栏。对应格子：{ref}`sdd-x-fence`、{ref}`tdd-x-fence`、{ref}`mdd-x-fence`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:101
#: ff4e0087a481449cb436cad906d1418c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Operating drumbeat.** Adopt the weekly entropy audit "
"(`_handson/06-operating-a-harness/entropy-audit.yml`) and the artefact state"
" model (`_handson/06-operating-a-harness/artefact-state-model.yaml`); these "
"harden the Groom row — {ref}`sdd-x-groom`, {ref}`tdd-x-groom`, {ref}`mdd-x-"
"groom`."
msgstr ""
"**运行节拍。** 采纳每周熵审计（`_handson/06-operating-a-harness/entropy-"
"audit.yml`）与制品状态机（`_handson/06-operating-a-harness/artefact-state-"
"model.yaml`）；这两件一起，把\"梳理\"那一行夯实 —— {ref}`sdd-x-groom`、{ref}`tdd-x-"
"groom`、{ref}`mdd-x-groom`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:107
#: 67b1eeb189114e76b9cf6be7e46004f1
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Forsgren, Humble & Kim's DORA-metrics work {cite}`forsgren2018accelerate` "
"argues that a quarterly cadence is the right unit for measurement; day 31–60"
" is the second month of your first quarter."
msgstr ""
"Forsgren、Humble 与 Kim 的 DORA 度量工作 {cite}`forsgren2018accelerate` "
"主张：季度节奏才是度量的合适单位；第 31–60 天就是你第一个季度的第二个月。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:111
#: 5e8367e3baef4ec48ee77c064b755949
msgid "Pitfall — The Day-60 \"row or column?\" paralysis"
msgstr "陷阱 —— 第 60 天 \"一行还是一列？\" 的瘫痪"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:114
#: a288cb08c98045ccaaa6573b95e4c9a1
msgid ""
"A team reaches Day 31 with one cell shipped and spends the next three weeks "
"in a committee debate: *row* or *column*? Which guardian? Which zone? By Day"
" 60 no second artefact has shipped; the team reports \"strategy work\" in "
"retro. **Why**: the row-or- column choice is optimisation theatre — either "
"direction is a real improvement, and the wrong choice (if one exists) is "
"recoverable in the next quarter. Time spent choosing is time not spent "
"shipping. **Fix**: pick the direction whose *weakest cell* is the most "
"embarrassing to name out loud. If you are ashamed to show a colleague your "
"`AGENTS.md` today, ship the full SDD row; if your CI fails intermittently "
"and nobody rotates the key that fixes it, ship the full Fence column. The "
"embarrassment test resolves the paralysis in five minutes and picks the "
"direction that was always going to matter most."
msgstr ""
"一支团队在第 31 天时已经交付了一格，接下来三周全耗在一场委员会辩论里：是 *一行* 还是 *一列*？哪位护法？哪一区域？到第 60 "
"天，第二件制品一件都没出；团队在回顾会上汇报\"战略工作\"。**为什么**：一行或一列，本身是一场\"优化剧场\"——任一方向都是真实改进，而\"错误选择\"（如果真有的话）在下一个季度都可救。选择时花掉的时间，就是没有交付的时间。**解法**：挑那个"
" *最弱格子* 最让你不好意思当众说出口的方向。如果今天把 `AGENTS.md` 给同事看你会脸红，就上完整 SDD 行；如果 CI "
"时不时挂、却没人去轮换那把能修它的密钥，就上完整护栏列。这个\"尴尬测试\"能在五分钟内解开这场瘫痪，并挑出那个原本就最重要的方向。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:130
#: 61c88e1da9384279b254ca922ace149a
msgid "Day 61–90 · A Production HarnessCard Review"
msgstr "Day 61–90 · 一次生产级 HarnessCard 评审"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:132
#: 6252f1cbd0c24919b16eabaadd6a6aa6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Run a full HarnessCard review on a production codebase using the blank "
"template from Appendix D (see {ref}`apd-harnesscard-template`), land at "
"least one harness-driven improvement, and record the measurable delta."
msgstr ""
"在一份生产代码库上，用附录 D 的空白模板（见 {ref}`apd-harnesscard-template`）跑一次完整 HarnessCard "
"评审，合入至少一项由挽具驱动的改进，并记录可度量的 delta。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:136
#: e5773a33c120417d8dd943451bd61055
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Score.** Fill the twelve-cell blank HarnessCard at {ref}`apd-harnesscard-"
"template` — every cell gets a 0–5 score and a one-line evidence note. Cross-"
"check against {ref}`sdd-x-bridle`, {ref}`tdd-x-fence`, and {ref}`mdd-x-"
"fence` using `_handson/11-lazy-ai-coder/HarnessCard-Act1.md` as a worked "
"precedent."
msgstr ""
"**打分。** 把 {ref}`apd-harnesscard-template` 里那张十二格的空白 HarnessCard 填满 —— 每格给出 "
"0–5 的分数与一行证据备注。用 `_handson/11-lazy-ai-coder/HarnessCard-Act1.md` 作为实例参考，跟 "
"{ref}`sdd-x-bridle`、{ref}`tdd-x-fence` 与 {ref}`mdd-x-fence` 交叉核对。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:142
#: 4e68dd3cae0c4ae1887c13ebf4bcae46
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Raise one cell.** Pick the lowest-scoring cell, land one fix scoped to it "
"(a `make` target, a hook, a YAML, a script — see `_handson/11-lazy-ai-"
"coder/reproduce.sh` for the worked pattern) and tie the fix back to the "
"target cell (e.g. {ref}`mdd-x-paddock`)."
msgstr ""
"**抬升一格。** 选得分最低的那一格，合入一项收束在这一格里的修复（一个 `make` 目标、一个钩子、一段 YAML、一段脚本 —— 以 "
"`_handson/11-lazy-ai-coder/reproduce.sh` 为已跑通的样板），并把这项修复绑回它所针对的那一格（例如 "
"{ref}`mdd-x-paddock`）。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:146
#: 8e243e7069544546a13f6b128fa918c6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Re-score and attach.** Author the post-fix HarnessCard using "
"`_handson/11-lazy-ai-coder/HarnessCard-Act4.md` as a template, attach it to "
"the release PR, and include a one-line delta note naming which cell moved "
"(e.g. {ref}`sdd-x-groom`) and by how much."
msgstr ""
"**重评并挂载。** 用 `_handson/11-lazy-ai-coder/HarnessCard-Act4.md` 作模板，写出修复后的 "
"HarnessCard，挂到发布 PR 上，并附一行 delta 备注：指名是哪一格在动（例如 {ref}`sdd-x-groom`）、动了多少。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:151
#: e19300aa72c6441c91356c3245a9af32
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Lehman's evolution laws {cite}`lehman1980laws` explain why a quarterly re-"
"score is not optional: unmaintained harnesses decay by default."
msgstr "Lehman 的演化定律 {cite}`lehman1980laws` 解释了\"季度重评\"为什么不是可选项：无人维护的挽具，默认就是会腐化。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:154
#: cda478d5912d4ae8b86e529eacb62b5b
msgid "Pitfall — Three ways the Day-90 review goes wrong"
msgstr "陷阱 —— 第 90 天评审会翻车的三种方式"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:157
#: c58975d597874ce7bcbab0d795cc97d2
msgid ""
"**Self-scored.** The engineer who shipped the fix also scores it; scores "
"drift up +0.5 on average. *Fix*: the Day-90 scorer is not the Day-30 "
"shipper."
msgstr "**自打分。** 交付修复的那位工程师同时也是打分人；分数平均偏移 +0.5。*解法*：第 90 天的打分人，不能是第 30 天的交付人。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:161
#: 4271e7e038e047d690f55134bc01bacb
msgid ""
"**Inputs not outcomes.** Cell scores rise while DORA metrics don't. Every "
"cell score must carry one outcome metric it is *predicted* to move (the "
"Ch.11 *vanity delta* pitfall develops this in full)."
msgstr ""
"**投入而非产出。** 格子得分在涨，DORA 指标却不动。每一项格子得分，都必须配一条它 *被预言要移动* 的产出指标（第 11 章的 *虚荣 "
"delta* 陷阱对此做了完整展开）。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:165
#: ee10d38d9c4c4005978ef8a5f862f9cd
msgid ""
"**Raising the top, not the bottom.** The team lifts a 4 to a 5 instead of a "
"1 to a 2; the mean rises but the weakest load-bearing dimension doesn't. "
"*Fix*: the Day-90 ritual must pick the lowest-scoring cell, even when a "
"stronger cell is tempting."
msgstr ""
"**抬高顶、不抬低底。** 团队把一个 4 抬成 5，而不是把一个 1 抬成 2；均值在升，承重最弱的那个维度却纹丝不动。*解法*：第 90 "
"天的仪式必须去挑得分最低的那一格，哪怕更强的某一格更诱人。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:171
#: ee8a1fcf8c0142caa9ade8ddcf7a3595
msgid "§12.3 — Open Questions"
msgstr "§12.3 —— 悬而未决的问题"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:173
#: 7b42f68c0dad468282da4f8f4712dc2e
msgid ""
"At most seven directions where the book raises questions it does not answer."
" Each carries at least one citation that sketches the adjacent literature."
msgstr "最多七个方向——在这些方向上，本书提出了自己并未回答的问题。每一条至少配一处引用，勾勒相邻文献。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:177
#: fd769448a9744170b158fe6ee7261081
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Meta-harness versioning under multi-tenant LLM deployments.** How should "
"harness rules survive a provider rolling out a model change mid-quarter, "
"especially when customers share a tenant? {cite}`huyen2025aieng`."
msgstr ""
"**多租户 LLM 部署下的元挽具版本化。** "
"当供应商在季度中段推送模型变更、尤其当多个客户共享同一租户时，挽具规则该如何存活？{cite}`huyen2025aieng`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:181
#: 2482dbe5c38c43d4ab878f32c4bf8e8c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**When to migrate from blog-format `.md` context into a structured RAG "
"pipeline.** Karpathy's context-engineering framing "
"{cite}`karpathy2025context` bears on this but does not resolve it."
msgstr ""
"**何时把博客体 `.md` 上下文迁移到结构化 RAG 管道。** Karpathy 的 context engineering 定义 "
"{cite}`karpathy2025context` 与此相关，但并没有给出答案。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:184
#: 88b1b48b7d1c49d6ad74d01164fa5806
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**HarnessCards for polyglot monorepos and cross-geography teams.** Does the "
"3 × 4 matrix survive scaling up the unit of analysis? {cite}`conway1968law`."
msgstr ""
"**多语言 monorepo 与跨地域团队的 HarnessCard。** 当分析单位被放大，这套 3 × 4 "
"矩阵还扛得住吗？{cite}`conway1968law`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:187
#: 2e4cb3d699ed43b18a53094d99247ad8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Continuous vs milestone-level entropy measurement.** Can entropy reduction"
" be measured continuously across a sprint, or is milestone measurement the "
"highest useful resolution? {cite}`lehman1980laws`."
msgstr ""
"**连续型 vs 里程碑型熵度量。** 熵的下降能在一次 sprint "
"中被连续度量吗？还是说\"按里程碑\"就已经是最高有用分辨率？{cite}`lehman1980laws`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:190
#: 6f9d52722b5a4986b9e18f38ac5d3acf
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Benchmarks that distinguish good harnesses from bad ones.** The Terminal-"
"Bench 2.0 data point is suggestive but not settled "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench`."
msgstr ""
"**能把好挽具与坏挽具区分开的基准测试。** Terminal-Bench 2.0 提供了一个暗示性的数据点，但尚未成为定论 "
"{cite}`langchain2026tbench`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:193
#: 9f060a21872743f2bc077033af2373be
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**HarnessCard disclosure requirements for safety-critical agents.** Should "
"regulators require HarnessCard-style disclosure the way they require SBOMs? "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition`."
msgstr ""
"**安全关键型智能体的 HarnessCard 披露要求。** 监管机构是否应像要求 SBOM 一样，要求 HarnessCard "
"式披露？{cite}`car2025decomposition`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:196
#: 80fb31ca05d94e04b76fb8d61e1dda40
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**The half-life of a skill.** How long does a `SKILL.md` keep its load-"
"bearing value before prompt drift erodes it? {cite}`anthropic2024skills`."
msgstr ""
"**一项技能的半衰期。** 在 prompt 漂移把一份 `SKILL.md` "
"侵蚀掉之前，它还能承重多久？{cite}`anthropic2024skills`。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:200
#: 210c292c60c8480f9ce4ac3680a1c013
msgid "§12.4 — What the book is *not* arguing"
msgstr "§12.4 —— 本书 *并未* 主张的事"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:202
#: 1130a26b6b4f429981d5fa47352c9862
msgid ""
"A reader who has made it this far deserves the honest footnote on what this "
"book's thesis does and does not claim."
msgstr "一位读到这里的读者，有资格拿到一则诚实的脚注——说明本书的主张所包含、以及 *不* 包含的东西。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:205
#: d9a9629394324e1185611fb44c05660b
msgid ""
"**Harnesses do not replace taste.** Nothing in the 3×4 matrix tells a team "
"*which problem is worth solving*, which architecture to adopt, or when a "
"`SKILL.md` is answering the wrong question. The harness constrains *how* the"
" agent writes code; it does not originate *what* code is worth writing. "
"Chapter 02's Stage-4 pitfall applies at the whole-book level."
msgstr ""
"**挽具不能替代品味。** 3×4 矩阵里没有一格会告诉一支团队 *哪个问题值得解决*、该采用何种架构、或某份 `SKILL.md` "
"在回答一个错问题。挽具约束的是\"智能体 *怎样* 写代码\"；它不产生\"*什么* 代码值得写\"。第 02 章 Stage-4 "
"的陷阱，在整本书层面同样成立。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:211
#: 936f3becb85940608c8bf45d144fb298
msgid ""
"**Not every team needs every cell.** The §03.5 *when not to use* section is "
"not a rhetorical concession; a solo prototype, a throwaway script, or a "
"frozen legacy system genuinely do not pay back the harness investment. A "
"team adopting the twelve-cell discipline for a forty-line CSV parser is "
"performing harness theatre whether they know it or not."
msgstr ""
"**并不是每支团队都需要每一格。** §03.5 "
"的\"何时不用\"并不是一段修辞让步；独自做的原型、一次性的脚本、一套被冻结的遗留系统，的确不会偿还这份挽具投资。一支为了一段四十行 CSV "
"解析器就去采用十二格纪律的团队，无论自觉与否，都在上演一场挽具剧场。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:217
#: 0ee8a7ec44504c38bcc92a0659f29ab2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**The naming is not settled.** The four-zone vocabulary is practitioner-"
"origin (§05.Provenance). If CAR {cite}`car2025decomposition` or LangChain's "
"five-part anatomy {cite}`langchain2026tbench` fits your team better, use "
"that framing and translate. The book's bet is on the *three-guardian × "
"twelve-cell decomposition* as a Monday-morning planning tool, not on the "
"zone names as a final taxonomy."
msgstr ""
"**命名并未板上钉钉。** 这份四区域词汇来自从业者（见 §05.Provenance）。若 CAR "
"{cite}`car2025decomposition` 或 LangChain 的五部分解剖 {cite}`langchain2026tbench` "
"更适合你的团队，就用那一套框架，并做翻译即可。本书押注的是 *三大护法 × 十二格分解* "
"作为\"周一早上可用的规划工具\"，并未押注\"这些区域名\"成为终极分类法。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:224
#: 98f0b5525852411182587932178e0666
msgid ""
"**The pitfalls are not exhaustive.** The inline callouts name the failures "
"the author has debugged, watched others debug, or read credible accounts of."
" They are a starting vocabulary, not a complete bestiary — §12.3 names where"
" new failure modes are most likely to surface next."
msgstr ""
"**那些陷阱并未穷尽。** 行内的 callout "
"只点出了作者自己调试过、看别人调试过、或读过可信记录的那些失败模式。它们是一份起步词汇表，不是一部完整异兽录——§12.3 "
"指出了下一轮新失败模式最可能冒出来的地方。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:230
#: e66cae1443b94e26a4010db84c654781
msgid ""
"If this chapter's 30/60/90 checklist, the 3×4 matrix, and the pitfall "
"vocabulary give your team one refused-commit event, one measured signal, and"
" one revised `AGENTS.md` bullet in the next ninety days, the book has done "
"its job."
msgstr ""
"若本章的 30/60/90 清单、3×4 矩阵、以及这份陷阱词汇表，能在接下来九十天里给你的团队带来：一次被拒的 commit "
"事件、一条被度量的信号、一条被修订过的 `AGENTS.md` 条目——那本书的活儿就算干完了。"

#: ../../source/chapters/12-where-we-go-from-here.md:235
#: 90c6d99ba5794d618a70372372061f08
